</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sorrentino</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The ryanodine receptors gene family: expression and functional meaning</article-title><source>Basic Appl Myol</source><year>2004</year><volume>14</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>343</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gromada</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jorgensen</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Dissing</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cyclic ADP-ribose and inositol 1,4,5-triphosphate mobilizes Ca<sup>2+</sup> from distinct intracellular pools in permeabilized lacrimal acinar cells</article-title><source>FEBS Lett </source><year>1995b</year><volume>360</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7883052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gromada</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jorgensen</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Dissing</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The release of intracellular Ca<sup>2+</sup> in lacrimal acinar cells by &#x003b1;-,&#x003b2;-adrenergic and muscarinic cholinergic stimulation: the roles of inositol trisphosphate and cyclic ADP-ribose</article-title><source>Pfluggers Arch </source><year>1995c</year><volume>429</volume><fpage>751</fpage><lpage>761</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thorn</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerasimenko</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Petersen</sur